---
import BackLink from '../components/BackLink.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="FAQ · yFu Temple"
	description="Credits for the yFu comic, the 2024 comic NFT, and how the yFu Temple relates to Yearn.">
	<div class="relative -mt-1 flex w-screen flex-col overflow-hidden p-0 md:p-6">
		<main class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-screen-xl" style="min-height: 100vh">
			<div>
				<div class="p-4 md:px-0">
					<BackLink href="/" label="HOME" />
				</div>
				<section class="w-full px-4 md:px-0">
					<div class="relative mb-10 flex flex-col border-2 border-white text-white">
						<div class="border-b-2 border-white p-8">
							<h1 class="whitespace-pre-wrap text-4xl font-bold text-white">F.A.Q.</h1>
							<div class="mt-10">
								<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What is yFu the comic?</h2>
								<ul class="mt-4 max-w-2xl list-outside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										yFu is a comic series in four books, each with 24 story pages, which tells the story of Yearn Finance's origination, DAO and philosophy, with an epic narrative set within the Pills universe.
									</li>
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										The project and lore was conceived by the YFI Story team at Yearn (Zemm, Pillhead, BigBadaboom, Pentacle and Banteg).
									</li>
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										yFu was written and produced by Devil's Due Studios: Story by Josh Blaylock, Art by Travis Hymel, Colors by Greg &amp; Fake, Letters by Shawn DePasquale.
									</li>
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										Additional development, design and technical support was provided by Major, Worms, Murderteeth, Pacific Design and yAcademy.
									</li>
								</ul>
							</div>

							<div class="mt-10">
								<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What was the yFu Comic NFT?</h2>
								<ul class="mt-4 max-w-2xl list-outside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										In 2024, a limited edition of 888 yFu Comic NFTs was minted on Base, each associated with a frame from the comics.
									</li>
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										Holders at the snapshot received a physical set of all four first edition comics, produced and shipped by Devil's Due Comics.
									</li>
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										The NFT contract is <a
											href="https://basescan.org/address/0x39adafad9fde221725b975b4adae8b8f2dfa6d4b"
											target="_blank"
											rel="noreferrer"><span class="underline hover:text-yearn-blue">0x39ad...6d4b</span></a>
									</li>
								</ul>
							</div>

							<div class="mt-10">
								<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">How is the yFu Temple affiliated with Yearn?</h2>
								<ul class="mt-4 max-w-2xl list-outside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										The yFu Temple was created in the process of developing the lore and characters in the yFu comic.
									</li>
									<li class="text-base text-white">
										It is managed by Yearn contributors currently. You can get involved by finding us in the<a
											href="https://discord.com/invite/yearn"
											target="_blank"
											rel="noreferrer"><span class="underline hover:text-yearn-blue"> Yearn Discord</span></a>
									</li>
								</ul>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</div>
</Layout>
